---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About HUDA, RIMO’s personal humanities and social-science blog.">
  <article class="simple-page page-frame">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>HUDA is RIMO’s personal blog.</h1>
      <p class="page-deck">
        A place for essays and notes across history, literature, philosophy, cinema, music,
        law, and sociology.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="simple-prose">
      <p>
        The name stays deliberately open. HUDA is not an institute, journal, or imagined academy.
        It is one person’s public notebook: a place to follow questions across disciplines while
        keeping arguments, sources, and revisions visible.
      </p>
      <h2>Reading here</h2>
      <p>
        Each piece has its own permanent address. Longer essays keep dates and terms near the
        opening, references at the end, and notes beside the relevant sentence when the screen
        allows it.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        The only public contact for this site is <a href={SITE.github}>RIMO’s GitHub profile</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
